inator of celebrating football's downtrodden, former Los Angeles columnist Steve Harvey, died last week.","published":"2026-11-18T13:23:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50519786/bottom-10-week-11-clemson-steve-harvey","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-18T11:39:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-18T16:13:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA-Michigan best bets: Look to the point total as Bruins head to Ann Arbor","description":"Let's find the best betting angle for UCLA-Michigan as the undefeated Bruins head to Ann Arbor.","published":"2026-11-18T12:15:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50513419/college-football-betting-week-12-michigan-ucla","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who could be the postseason and CFP X factors?","description":"Breaking down postseason X factors for every CFP top-25 team.","published":"2026-11-18T11:45:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510750/cfp-top-25-postseason-x-factor","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"QB rankings for all 68 Power 4 college football teams","description":"We're nearing the end of the season. How have our opinions about the top quarterbacks changed?","published":"2026-11-18T11:43:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510847/ranking-power-4-qbs","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL mock draft: Reid's midseason first-round predictions for all 32 picks","description":"Which NFL team could land Drew Mestemaker? Who needs Chris Cole, Ashton Hampton or Jamari Johnson? Jordan Reid projected first-round picks for 2027 -- and a trade.","published":"2026-11-18T16:28:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50502243/2027-nfl-mock-draft-reid-midseason-32-first-round-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5112674/bryant-wesco-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryant_Wesco"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Bryant Wesco","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryant_Wesco","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:24Z","intro":"Bryant Wesco Jr. (born September 22, 2005) is an American college football wide receiver for the Clemson Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wesco was born on September 22, 2005, and grew up in Midlothian, Texas. He attended Midlothian High School, where he competed in football and track. After playing on the freshman football team in 2020, he made the varsity as a sophomore in 2021 and made 17 receptions for 212 yards and four touchdowns. As a junior in 2022, he recorded 56 receptions for 1,072 yards and 12 touchdowns, despite Midlothian using a run-heavy playbook. In his senior year, Wesco caught 36 passes for 619 yards and 13 touchdowns, despite appearing in just seven games. He concluded his high school career having totaled 109 catches for 1,903 yards and 29 touchdowns, averaging 17.5 yards-per-reception.\nWesco was invited to the Under Armour All-America Game and to the Polynesian Bowl. A five-star prospect, he was a consensus top 35 recruit in the nation and was ranked in the top 25 by PrepStar (15), 247Sports (22) and ESPN (25). He committed to play college football for the Clemson Tigers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wesco entered Clemson as an early enrollee in January 2024. He received his first start in the second game of the season and caught a 76-yard touchdown pass against Appalachian State."}]}}